    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d735">

                <pb facs="1173" n="1077" sameAs="frus:frus1874/pg1077"/>

                <head>No. 732.<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Hall to Mr. Fish.</hi></head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Telgram.]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Havana</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1873-11-18"><hi rendition="#italic">November</hi> 18, 1873</date>.
                        (Received Nov. 18—10.10 p.m.)</dateline></opener>
                <p>The consul at Santiago de Cuba reports, under date 13th instant? that the total
                    number of executions of persons from the Virginius was <pb facs="1174" n="1078"
                        xml:id="pg1078"/> fifty-three, and that there had been no executions since
                    8th instant Statements published here on 14th instant respecting fifty-seven
                    additional executions prove untrue. The British steamer Niobe was at Santiago,
                    and the Wyoming expected there on the 14th. The Virginius arrived here
                    to-day.</p>
                <closer><signed>HALL.</signed></closer>
            </div>
